given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>McClish</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>An international comparison of physicians&#x02019; judgments of outcome rates of cardiac procedures and attitudes toward risk, uncertainty, justifiability, and regret</article-title><source>Med Decis Making</source><year>1998</year><volume>18</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>140</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Poses RM, De Saintonge DM, McClish DK, et al. An international comparison of physicians&#x02019; judgments of outcome rates of cardiac procedures and attitudes toward risk, uncertainty, justifiability, and regret. Med Decis Making. 1998;18(2):131&#x02013;40, Apr&#x02013;Jun. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9566446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Levenkron</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Suchman</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Manchester</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does physician uncertainty affect patient satisfaction?</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>1988</year><volume>3</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>144</fpage><lpage>149</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF02596120</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Johnson CG, Levenkron JC, Suchman AL, Manchester R. Does physician uncertainty affect patient satisfaction? J Gen Intern Med. 1988;3(2):144&#x02013;9, Mar&#x02013;Apr. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3357071</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keating</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Landon</surname><given-names